---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — AgentSutra"
  description="What AgentSutra collects, deliberately does not collect and keeps out of the public publication."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-intro__grid shell">
      <p class="page-intro__context">Publication policy</p>
      <div>
        <h1>Privacy</h1><p class="page-intro__lead">
          The first release is intentionally small: no accounts, tracking scripts, comments or
          behavioural profiles.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Website visitors</h2>
      <p>
        AgentSutra does not set first-party advertising cookies, create user accounts or run
        client-side analytics in the initial publication. The hosting and network providers
        necessarily process request metadata such as IP address, user agent and timestamp to deliver
        and protect the site under their own policies.
      </p>
      <h2>Publication evidence</h2>
      <p>
        Private evidence stays outside this repository and website. Public notes must not contain
        credentials, client names, hostnames, IP addresses, personal filesystem paths, private
        runbooks or raw infrastructure topology.
      </p>
      <h2>External links and platforms</h2>
      <p>
        Links to sources and AgentSutra adaptations on other platforms take you to services with
        their own privacy practices. Those services are distribution surfaces; agentsutra.dev
        remains the canonical publication.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If measurement is introduced later, this page will be updated before collection begins, with
        the narrow purpose, provider, retention and opt-out position stated plainly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
